                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in \Omega^3_+(X)
              is locally gauge equivalent to the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo +
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma|_U = f^\ast \phi + \mathbf{d}\beta
            %p
              via a 2-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bryant05"} Bryant 05, p. 21
          %p
            This follows from the fact, remark
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Definition3FormsGiveOpenSubset"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
            inside all 3-forms: given a chart centered around any point then there is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}\beta
            vanishing at that point such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
