                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma|_U \simeq f^\ast \phi + \mathbf{d}\beta
            at that point. But since the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(7)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            is open, there is an open neighbourhood around that point where this is still the case.
          #AtlasForClosedG2tructureInTermsOfHigherGeometry.num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              When regarding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              in the wider context of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedG2StructureByAtlas"}
              corresponds to a diagram of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+infinity-groupoids"} formal smooth infinity-groupoids
              of the following form:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 7
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi β
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi σ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 3
                            %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; U
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}^7 &amp;&amp; \swArrow_{\mathrlap{\beta}} &amp;&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\phi}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\sigma}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}^3\mathbb{R}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}^3\mathbb{R}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} higher moduli stack
              of flat 3-forms with 2-form gauge transformations between them (and 1-form gauge transformation between these). The diagram expresses the 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              as a map to this moduli stack, which when restricted to the cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              becomes gauge equivalent to the pullback of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
              (of maps of formal smooth
              = succeed "-groupoids)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
