                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
              if it carries a 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              with the relation of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#G2manifold"}
              generalized to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{d} \omega
                    \\;=\;
                    \\lambda \star \omega
            %p and hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{d} \star \omega
                    \\;=\;
                    0
            %p
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda = 0
              this reduces to strict
              = succeed "-holonomy," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#G2manifold"}
          %p (See for instance Bilal &amp; Derendinger-Sfetsos 02Bilal &amp; Metzger 03](#BilalMetzger03).)
          %h4#WithADEOrbifoldStructure With ADE orbifold structure
          %p
            When used as
            = succeed "-fibers" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} phenomenology
            one needs to consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+orbifolds"} ADE orbifolds
            with “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            \-manifold” structure, i.e.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-orbifolds"} G₂-orbifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %em Joyce orbifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            purposes this
            = succeed "-orbifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fibration
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3+surface"} K3 surface
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K3}
          %p
            For instance, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K3} \times T^3
            admits a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} SO(3)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the tangent spaces of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mn 3
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K3} \times T^3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K3}
            by rotation of the
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyper-K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} hyper-Kähler manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K_3}
            and on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^3
            by the standard rotation. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_{ADE}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_{K3}\times T^3)/K_{ADE}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-orbifold"} G₂-orbifold
            (
            %a{:href => "#Acharya98"}> Acharya 1098, p.3
            ). For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_{ADE}
            %em not
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            then this has precisely one
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+spinor"} parallel spinor
          %p
            In a local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K3}
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2
            the orbifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{K3}/K_{ADE}
            locally looks like
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi ADE
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2/{G_{ADE}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{ADE}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-orbifolds"} G₂-orbifolds
            are discussed in some detail by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah &amp; Witten 2001
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Reidegeld15"} Reidegeld 2015
          %p
            Codimension-4 ADE singularities in
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            %a{:href => "AcharyaGukov04"} Acharya &amp; Gukov 2004, section 5.1
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Barrett06"} Barrett 2006
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#existence Existence
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A 7-manifold admits a
              = succeed "-structure," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#G2Structure"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
              and a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
          %p
            That orientability and spinnability is necessary follows directly from the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2 \hookrightarrow GL(7)
            is connected and simply connected. That these conditions are already sufficient is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Gray69"}> Gray 69
            ), see also (
            %a{:href => "#Bryant05"}> Bryant 05, remark 3
            ).
          %h3#metric_structure Metric structure
          %p
            The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            manifold is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricci+tensor"} Ricci flat
            = succeed "-holonomy," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WeakG2Holonomy"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifold"} Einstein manifold
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            = succeed "." do
